{title: 074 - Like a River Glorious}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #074 • WYE VALLEY • 11.11.12.11}
{lyricist: Frances R. Havergal}
{composer: James Mountain}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 74}
{meta: tune WYE VALLEY}
{meta: meter 11.11.12.11}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]Like a [Gm]river [F]glorious [Bb/F]Is God's [Edim]perfect [F]peace,
[F/A]Over [Gm]all victorious [C/G]In its [Dm/F]bright increase;
[Am]Perfect, yet [C7/Bb]it floweth [C]Fuller [C7]every [C]day,
[F/C]Perfect, [Gm/Bb]yet it [Dm/A]groweth [F/C]Deeper [Gm/Bb]all the [Dm/A]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Am]Stayed upon [C7]Jehovah, [Gm/D]hearts [C7]are [F/C]fully [C]blessed
[F/C]Finding, [Gm/Bb]as [A7]He [Dm/A]promised, [F]perfect [Gm/Bb]peace and [F]rest.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]Hidden [Gm]in the [F]hollow [Bb/F]of His [Edim]blessed hand,
[F/A]Never [Gm]foe can [F]follow, [C/G]never [Dm/F]traitor [C/E]stand;
[Am]Not a [C7/Bb]surge of [Bb]worry, [Gm/D]not [C7]a [F/C]shade of [C]care,
[F/C]Not a [Gm/Bb]blast of [Dm/A]hurry [F/C]touch [Am]the [Gm/Bb]spirit [Dm/A]there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]Every [Gm]joy [F]or trial [Bb/F]falleth [Edim]from above,
[F/A]Traced upon [Gm]our [F]dial by [C/G]the Sun [Dm/F]of Love;
[Am]We may [C7/Bb]trust Him [Bb]fully [Gm/D]all [C7]for [F/C]us to [C]do.
[F/C]They who [Gm/Bb]trust Him [Dm/A]wholly [F/C]find [Am]Him [Gm/Bb]wholly [Dm/A]true.
{end_of_verse}
